Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:49:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] sm120: route low-M bf16 dense GEMMs to tuned Triton
 split-K kernel

cuBLAS-under-capture serves the qwen4 decode projections at 60-75% of DRAM
bandwidth on sm120; the SM100 CuTeDSL/split-K paths need tcgen05. The Triton
kernel reaches ~90% on the fused GDN in_proj (n=16480: 54.7us vs 49.3us floor,
was 65.9us). Verify graph 14.43 -> 13.79 ms/replay; C1 greedy median 142.8 ->
147.9 tok/s. Gated by SGLANG_ENABLE_SM120_LOWM_BF16_GEMM (default on, sm120
only, disabled under deterministic inference).

